    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Parts of the body"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "With the body, Spanish uses **el, la, los, las**, not mi or tu, whenever it is clear whose body it is: levanta **la** mano; tengo **las** piernas cansadas; me duele **la** espalda.\n\n**La mano** is feminine: la mano derecha, las manos frías.\n\n**Derecho** and **izquierdo** agree with the part: el pie **derecho**, la mano **derecha**, el brazo **izquierdo**, la pierna **izquierda**.\n\n**El dedo** is a finger and also a toe: los dedos de la mano, los dedos del pie."
      }
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": {"en": "At the gym"},
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Monitor",
          "es": "Levanta los brazos.",
          "en": "Raise your arms.",
          "analisis": [["Levanta", "command (tú)"], ["los brazos", "object"]]
        },
        {"quien": "Pablo", "es": "¿Los dos?", "en": "Both?", "analisis": [["¿Los dos?", "question"]]},
        {
          "quien": "Monitor",
          "es": "Sí. Ahora la mano derecha en la rodilla izquierda.",
          "en": "Yes. Now your right hand on your left knee.",
          "analisis": [["Ahora", "time"], ["la mano derecha", "object"], ["en la rodilla izquierda", "place"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Tengo las piernas cansadas.",
          "en": "My legs are tired.",
          "analisis": [["Tengo", "verb"], ["las piernas", "object"], ["cansadas", "description"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Monitor",
          "es": "La espalda recta y la cabeza alta.",
          "en": "Back straight and head up.",
          "analisis": [["La espalda recta", "instruction"], ["la cabeza alta", "instruction"]]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "¡Y tengo los pies fríos!",
          "en": "And my feet are cold!",
          "analisis": [["tengo", "verb"], ["los pies", "object"], ["fríos", "description"]]
        }
      ]
    },
